74320501089096, -0.02354975789785385, -0.011994021013379097, 0.07218607515096664, -0.015254278667271137, -0.019685838371515274, -0.038708802312612534, 0.04286627471446991, -0.002155903959646821, 0.04087623208761215, -0.015396212227642536, 0.011406218633055687, 0.03506746515631676, -0.04168989881873131, 0.044041477143764496, -0.05869155749678612, -0.047234293073415756, -0.026278920471668243, -0.08524811267852783, 0.008236046880483627, -0.11017387360334396, 0.010986628010869026, -0.04159574583172798, -6.214683878624783e-08, 0.08850455284118652, -0.002523137954995036, 0.03454827889800072, 0.04487637057900429, 0.006196192465722561, -0.019232874736189842, 0.02085251174867153, 0.026874301955103874, 0.1084071472287178, 0.0023798660840839148, 0.03944046050310135, -0.020185869187116623, -0.1094040647149086, -0.004563667345792055, 0.0006393198273144662, 0.0830785259604454, 0.05166083574295044, -0.03686290234327316, -0.05031736195087433, 0.08530732989311218, -0.0719519779086113, 0.01220092736184597, -0.08024073392152786, 0.028887508437037468, 0.0644184947013855, 0.033791013062000275, 0.057402029633522034, 0.016918502748012543, 0.0893639624118805, 0.08441232889890671, 0.02450736239552498, -0.015671057626605034, 0.07897719740867615, -0.04153870418667793, -0.0609796941280365, 0.022443508729338646, 0.06698844581842422, 0.004243341740220785, 0.02319003827869892, 0.037556689232587814, 0.01536940410733223, 0.02754661999642849, 0.08176179230213165, 0.012584230862557888, 0.021916363388299942, -0.03859640285372734, -0.002327224938198924, -0.05096042901277542, 0.03931327909231186, 0.08069371432065964, -0.08710353821516037, 0.012203570455312729, -0.006564723327755928, 0.055931221693754196, 0.0510382317006588, 0.02636091411113739, 0.023102808743715286, 0.05585375800728798, 0.03199475258588791, -0.05418720096349716, 0.037166498601436615, 0.07628428190946579, -0.058969929814338684, 0.059250276535749435]], "documents": ["Google Play Location Permissions Policy ======================================== 1. FOREGROUND LOCATION: Apps may access location in the foreground if the user has granted ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION or ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION. A visible indicator must be shown while location is being accessed. 2. BACKGROUND LOCATION: Apps targeting API 29+ must request foreground location FIRST. Background location requires a separate, explicit grant by the user. 3. PRECISION: Apps should only request ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION if precise location is necessary for core functionality. Otherwise, use ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION. 4. TRANSPARENCY: Location usage must be disclosed in the app's privacy policy and store listing. 5. NO SILENT TRACKING: Apps must not track user location without clear visible indication. Background location access must show a persistent notification. 6. JUSTIFICATION: Developers must provide a clear rationale to users before requesting any location permission. The rationale must explain how location data is used.", "Google Play Microphone and Camera Policy ========================================== 1. USER INITIATED: Apps must only access the microphone or camera when the user has explicitly triggered the feature. No background recording or capturing is allowed. 2. VISIBLE INDICATOR: Whenever the microphone or camera is active, a clear visual indicator must be shown to the user. This can be a recording icon or status bar notification. 3. NO BACKGROUND ACCESS: Apps must not record audio or capture camera footage when running in the background. Any attempt to do so will result in immediate removal from the Play Store. 4. DISCLOSURE: Microphone and camera usage must be clearly disclosed in the app's privacy policy and in the Play Store listing. 5. MINIMAL ACCESS: Apps should only request microphone or camera permissions if the feature is essential to the app's core functionality. Permission requests must be contextual and timed to when the feature is actually needed. 6. DATA HANDLING: Any audio or video captured must be handled securely. Developers must disclose how this data is stored, transmitted, and whether it is shared with third parties.", "Google Play SMS and Call Log Policy =================================== Apps that request SMS or call log permissions must meet ALL of the following requirements: 1. CORE FUNCTIONALITY: SMS/call features must be the primary purpose of the app. Utility apps that only occasionally use SMS (e.g., for OTP) should use intent-based approaches instead. 2. USER CONSENT: Every SMS send must be preceded by a clear, visible confirmation dialog showing: - The recipient number - The message content - An explicit Send button 3. NO AUTO-SEND: Apps must never send SMS automatically without user action. Background SMS sending is prohibited and will result in immediate removal. 4. DISCLOSURE: The app's store listing must clearly state that SMS functionality is present and explain why it is needed. 5. CALL LOG ACCESS: Reading or writing call logs is restricted to default phone apps only. Third-party apps must not request READ_CALL_LOG or WRITE_CALL_LOG permissions. 6. RECEIVING SMS: Only the default SMS app may listen for incoming SMS messages. Third-party apps must not use RECEIVE_SMS permission.", "Google Play User Data Policy ============================== 1. CONTACTS ACCESS: Apps that request READ_CONTACTS or WRITE_CONTACTS must clearly justify why contact access is needed for core app functionality. Usage must be disclosed in the privacy policy. 2. MINIMAL DATA COLLECTION: Apps must only collect user data that is necessary for the stated functionality. Collecting excess data is a policy violation. 3. PRIVACY POLICY: All apps that collect user data must have a valid privacy policy linked in the Play Store listing. The policy must clearly explain what data is collected and how it is used. 4. DATA STORAGE: User data must be stored securely. Sensitive data must be encrypted both in transit and at rest. 5. THIRD PARTY SHARING: Apps must clearly disclose if user data is shared with third parties. Users must be given the option to opt out where possible. 6. PHONE STATE: Apps requesting READ_PHONE_STATE must justify the need based on core functionality. Simply reading device identifiers without clear purpose is not permitted. 7. EXTERNAL STORAGE: Reading or writing external storage requires clear justification. Apps must not access files outside their own app directory without explicit user consent."], "metadatas": [{"source": "location_policy.txt"}, {"source": "microphone_camera_policy.txt"}, {"source": "sms_call_policy.txt"}, {"source": "user_data_policy.txt"}]}